      "comments": [
        {
          "author": "Trikolon",
          "path": "nav-tracking-mitigations/stateful-client-bounce.sub.https.html",
          "line": 46,
          "commit_id": "103fa75652b4d1a03b10e5b88b7904ee587e836e",
          "review_state": "CHANGES_REQUESTED",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/47856#discussion_r1757027151",
          "body": "Why is a `while` loop required here? Is it because the bounce tracker classification only runs after a delay (on extended navigation end)? Right now that delay is implementation defined, but the spec recommends 10 seconds. \r\nEven if we're okay with waiting for 10 seconds, we should not spin the CPU for that long here. We can either add wait or make`run_bounce_tracking_mitigations` skip the 10 second wait.\r\n\r\nThe other way for an extended navigation to end (as per the spec) is if the user navigates again (before the 10 second timeout). We probably want to test both cases. I don't want to require it here since this is just the first basic bounce tracking mitigation test.",
          "fixed_before_merge": true
        },
        {
          "author": "Trikolon",
          "path": "nav-tracking-mitigations/stateful-client-bounce.sub.https.html",
          "line": 22,
          "commit_id": "103fa75652b4d1a03b10e5b88b7904ee587e836e",
          "review_state": "CHANGES_REQUESTED",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/47856#discussion_r1757034255",
          "body": "This seems overly complicated, can't you just await the load / link getter and then continue? Is there a specific reason why you need to resolve a promise externally?",
          "fixed_before_merge": true
        },
